{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For He spoke</b> — with will and desire, not by means of an instrument." "<b>He commanded and it stood</b> — the sense is doubled, as if he said: \"For He spoke and it was — He spoke.\"" "<b>And He commanded</b> — a command." "<b>And it stood</b> — as I explained in the manner of וברך ולא אשיבנה (\"and I will bless and not revoke it\"), for the power of HaShem is in the power of every agent, past or future."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:19.331626266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}